==English==

===Etymology===
From [[un-]] + [[roll]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To [[straighten]] something that has been [[roll]]ed, [[twist]]ed or [[curl]]ed.
#: ''Unroll your sleeping bag and spread it on the floor of the tent.''
# {{intransitive}} To [[emerge]], be [[reveal]]ed or become [[apparent]]; to [[unfold]].
#: ''We will have to see how the events '''unroll'''.''
# {{transitive}} {{computing}} To replace (a [[loop]] in a [[program]]) with a [[repetitive]] [[sequence]] of the individual [[instruction]]s that the loop would carry out, sometimes used as an [[optimization]].

====Related terms====
* [[unfold]]
* [[unfurl]]

